   {
    "text": "<<The Floods of Donnell>>\n\nIn the heart of Donnell, where the rivers run wild,  \nThe earth has been swallowed by the rising tide.  \nThe skies weep rain in a relentless tide,  \nAs the land is claimed by the waters that rise.\n\nThe fields once green now lie in a muddy bed,  \nWith roots and debris, a silent, broken bed.  \nThe people gather in the town square,  \nTheir faces etched with fear and the weight of the flood.\n\nThe river, once a guardian, now a beast,  \nIts course unchained, its fury unbound.  \nThe homes, the roads, the very air,  \nAre now part of the storm that has come.\n\nBut in the midst of the chaos, hope still burns,  \nA flicker in the dark, a light in the storm.  \nFor in the heart of Donnell, the fight continues,  \nAs the floodwaters rise, and the land is tested.\n\nSo let the floods be a lesson, a warning,  \nA reminder that nature can be both cruel and kind.  \nFor in the wake of the storm, new beginnings may rise,  \nAnd the people of Donnell will rise again.",
